---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="ManifestKit's privacy policy: what data is collected, what analytics or ads are used, and what happens to the text you type into a tool."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="byline">Last updated 2026-09-06</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Every generator on {SITE.name} runs entirely in your browser. Whatever you type into a
      form — a skill description, an MCP server name, rule content — is processed locally with
      plain JavaScript and never sent to a server. Closing the tab discards it; nothing is stored
      unless you click download. Separately, this site uses Google Analytics to see aggregate
      traffic (see below).
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses <a href="https://marketingplatform.google.com/about/analytics/" rel="noopener">Google Analytics</a>
      (GA4) to understand aggregate traffic — which pages get visited, roughly where from, and
      how often. Google Analytics sets its own cookies to do this and processes data under
      Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
      It has no connection to the tool forms above: what you type into a generator is never sent
      to Google or anywhere else.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site does collect</h2>
    <p>
      Standard web server logs (IP address, user agent, requested URL) are recorded automatically
      by the hosting provider for security and reliability, the same as almost any website. If
      this site displays advertising (via Google AdSense) in the future, that provider will also
      set cookies and collect data under its own privacy policy — this page will be updated
      before that happens.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Aside from the Google Analytics cookies described above, this site does not set cookies of
      its own. Your browser's local storage may be used purely to remember your own preferences
      on a page (nothing account-related); that data never leaves your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: see the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  article {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }
  .byline {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
